 "sentences": [
  {
   "text": "Pablo Escobar's hippos are still alive.",
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 2.3
  },
  {
   "text": "And Colombia has approved killing more than eighty of them.",
   "start": 2.96,
   "end": 5.14
  },
  {
   "text": "To understand why, you have to go back to 1981.",
   "start": 5.52,
   "end": 7.94
  },
  {
   "text": "Escobar imports four hippos.",
   "start": 8.64,
   "end": 10.28
  },
  {
   "text": "His estate sits between Medell\u00edn and Bogot\u00e1.",
   "start": 10.82,
   "end": 13.04
  },
  {
   "text": "In 1993 he dies, and they escape.",
   "start": 13.5,
   "end": 16.08
  },
  {
   "text": "By 2007, sixteen.",
   "start": 16.82,
   "end": 17.86
  },
  {
   "text": "By 2014, about forty.",
   "start": 18.68,
   "end": 20.53
  },
  {
   "text": "Now, around two hundred.",
   "start": 21.14,
   "end": 22.473
  },
  {
   "text": "But conservationists call them invasive.",
   "start": 22.92,
   "end": 24.44
  },
  {
   "text": "So Colombia approves killing over eighty.",
   "start": 25.12,
   "end": 26.7
  },
  {
   "text": "An Indian billionaire offers them shelter in India.",
   "start": 26.8,
   "end": 29.58
  },
  {
   "text": "Some ecologists say they should stay.",
   "start": 30.26,
   "end": 31.64
  },
  {
   "text": "Escobar is gone, but his hippos are not.",
   "start": 32.26,
   "end": 34.72
  }
 ]
